    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A kingdom founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> in 1139 whose border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, fixed in 1297, is among the oldest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>Its navigators reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#india">India</a> by sea in 1498 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#brazil">Brazil</a> in 1500, creating an empire of trading posts and colonies.</li><li>After union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#spain">Spain</a> (1580–1640), loss of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#brazil">Brazil</a> and civil war, the monarchy was overthrown by a revolution in 1910.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Between 1808 and 1821 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> was the seat of the Portuguese monarchy, the only time a European kingdom was ruled from one of its colonies.</p></aside>
    </section>

